nodes.summary:
- Purpose and scope: Article F of the PepsiCo Pension Equalization Plan – 409A Program covers U.K. Supplementary Appendix participants who perform U.S. service. It specifies that benefits for such individuals are determined under Section F.3, paid according to the plan’s standard time and form rules, and are subject to Internal Revenue Code section 409A. The Article was restated effective January 1, 2016; the original version was effective January 1, 2011 and applied to service before 2016.
- Definition of “Covered U.K. Employee”: A participant in the PepsiCo U.K. Pension Plan who:
  - Becomes subject to U.S. income taxes by transferring to a U.S. position or otherwise (“Engages in U.S. Service”);
  - Continues to accrue benefits under the PepsiCo U.K. Pension Plan after engaging in U.S. service;
  - Would have accrued benefits under the U.K. Supplementary Pension Appendix for that period but for the unavailability of accruals while engaging in U.S. service;
  - Subsequently either (A) is localized in the U.S. as an employee of the PepsiCo Organization, or (B) terminates employment with the PepsiCo Organization before beginning an assignment outside the U.S. (as defined in the Code);
  - And, after satisfying the above conditions, is designated by the company (designation language truncated in the excerpt).
- Administration notes: References Section F.3 for benefit determination methodology; reinforces compliance with Section 409A and adherence to standard plan payment provisions.
